<title>GERMANY: Buba declines comment on Bonn's revaluation plans.</title>
<headline>Buba declines comment on Bonn's revaluation plans.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Friday that it had no additional comment on the German government's plans to revalue central bank reserves.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no further comments beyond what we said on Thursday,&quot; said a Bundesbank spokesman in response to a Reuters enquiry.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said a revaluation of gold reserves could have an impact on the country's 1997 budget if the central bank made an interim account this year.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
